2. Full ast_builder.cpp using the generic rule-index approach? That's the hand-holding. I could instead give a *small but complete* implementation for a SUBSET and a recipe to extend — e.g., implement everything except some expression families (cast/assignment/condition/statement variants), leaving clear TODO stubs that return an "Unknown" node so it compiles and dumps. Then they extend family by family, and each time re-run and see real AST. This is a great iterative workflow: compile early, extend mechanically.

